  "raw": {
    "https://udayton.edu/careers/index.php": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers at UD : University of Dayton, Ohio Skip to content /////// Careers at UD Home Come Fly With Us Founded in 1850, the University of Dayton is a top-tier Catholic research university. Here, we adapt to meet the needs of the changing world. We turn big dreams into bold moves. And we build vibrant, inclusive and diverse communities that are marked by openness, cooperation, collegiality and a sense of service. Diverse experiences and backgrounds are vital to enriching our learning environment, advancing innovation, thinking critically and creatively, and solving complex problems. We're passionately striving to create a brighter tomorrow — together. View Staff and Faculty Jobs View Student Jobs Subscribe to Job Alerts Join Our Talent Network A Vibrant, Welcoming Community About UD UD is rooted in faith and dedicated to the common good. We invite people with diverse talents, interests and backgrounds to advance our common mission. Learn More About UD Explore the City of Dayton Add 423 Scenic Acres to Your Career Path Benefits Our competitive, flexible benefits help you achieve your goals and bring balance to your work — and the rest of your life. Explore Benefits Dual Career Resources We are pleased to provide support for spouses of prospective and newly hired faculty. While we cannot guarantee placement, we serve as an effective resource and support system for your spouse. Explore Dual Career Resources Disability Accommodation The University aims to increase access and inclusion for individuals with disabilities; reasonable accommodations may be provided upon request. Applicants can contact the Office of Human Resources at hr@udayton.edu or 937-229-2541 to obtain more information or request accommodation. Read the Accommodations Policy Nondiscrimination Policy The University of Dayton is committed to providing an educational and employment environment that is free from discrimination, and in compliance with federal and state laws. Read Nondiscrimination Policy Research for the Common Good UDRI The University of Dayton Research Institute is a globally recognized leader in research, development and transition of technologies that advance science and benefit the world. UDRI addresses the mission-critical needs of the Department of Defense and private industry while setting the standard for tomorrow's breakthroughs. Explore Careers at UDRI Contact Human Resources 300 College Park Dayton, Ohio                        45469 - 1649 937-229-2541 email Linkedin Campus Security and Fire Safety Report UD reports crime and fire statistics as required by federal law. The Annual Fire Safety and Security Report outlines reportable statistics and measures taken to protect the campus community, as well as institutional policies and programs related to safety and security. View Report Take the Next Step Apply for Jobs Subscribe to Job Alerts Join Our Talent Network Explore Majors and Programs Academic Calendar Careers Libraries News Next Steps Request Info Apply Visit Give Connect Facebook X Instagram Youtube Linkedin Directions Contact Us 300 College Park Dayton, Ohio 45469 937-229-1000 info@udayton.edu Porches Policies Safety Report a Concern Privacy Nondiscrimination Compliance"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/875/cw/en-us/listing/": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Employment Opportunities : University of Dayton, Ohio Home About Academics Admission Financial Aid Diversity Research Life at Dayton Athletics We Soar University Overview Catholic, Marianist Education Points of Pride Mission and Identity History Partnerships Location Faculty and Staff Directory Social Media Directory We Soar Academics Overview Program Listing Academic Calendar College of Arts and Sciences School of Business Administration School of Education and Health Sciences School of Engineering School of Law Professional and Continuing Education Intensive English Program University Libraries Admission Overview Undergraduate Transfer UD Sinclair Academy International Graduate Law Professional and Continuing Education Campus Visit Affordability Overview Undergraduate Transfer International Graduate Law Consumer Information Diversity Overview Office of Diversity and Inclusion Equity Compliance Office Research Overview Momentum: Our Research UD Research Institute Office for Research Technology Transfer Campus Overview Arts and Culture Campus Recreation City of Dayton Clubs and Organizations Housing and Dining Student Resources and Services Athletics Overview Dayton Flyers We Soar Overview Priorities Goals Impact Stories Volunteer Make a Gift Next Steps Apply Schedule a Visit Request Info Give Info For: Select Audience Alumni and Friends Current Students Future Students High School Counselors International Students Parents Faculty and Staff Select Audience Explore More News Academic Calendar Event Calendar Libraries Careers Employment Opportunities Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Department Open Date Close Date Part-Time Catering Services Attendant II Dining Serv - Catering - 800618 September 03, 2026 We are looking for individuals with diverse talents and backgrounds to join our nationally recognized team that is committed to providing exciting and healthy food options to students, faculty and staff on campus. We offer excellent benefits including paid leave and tuition assistance. The University of Dayton is proud to be named the Best Place to Work in the annual Best of Dayton contest. Part-Time Catering Services Attendant I Dining Serv - Catering - 800618 September 03, 2026 We are looking for individuals with diverse talents and backgrounds to join our nationally recognized team that is committed to providing exciting and healthy food options to students, faculty and staff on campus. We offer excellent benefits including paid leave and tuition assistance. The University of Dayton is proud to be named the Best Place to Work in the annual Best of Dayton contest. AM Design Engineer Adv Mfg Engineering - 250714 September 03, 2026 September 17, 2026 Are you interested in working for UDRI, a national leader in scientific and engineering research, serving government, industry and nonprofit customers? UDRI contributes to the fulfillment of the University’s commitments to education, research and public service through the involvement of students, faculty, Staff, and external partners. Established as the research arm of the University of Dayton in 1956, UDRI achieved $2.75 billion in cumulative sponsored research in 2020. We invite qualified candidates to apply for our AM Engineer opening! This full time and benefit eligible position offers health, dental and vision insurance, retirement, disability, tuition assistance for you and your dependents, vacation, sick, and holiday pay. Apply today! Assistant Professor of Practice or Lecturer specializing in Construction Engineering and Management SoE Exper Learning & Stdnt Success - 220100 September 02, 2026 October 18, 2026 Calling all Construction Engineering and Management Professionals:\n\nAre you interested in bringing your practical knowledge and experience in Construction Engineering and Management to educating the next generation of professionals?  Are you interested in developing unique practices and new experiential learning strategies? Are you looking for a university that educates the whole person and integrates learning and scholarship with leadership and service?\n\t\nIf so, the Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering and Engineering Mechanics at the University of Dayton, located in Dayton, OH invites you to apply for a faculty position as an Assistant Professor of Practice or Lecturer specializing in Construction Engineering and Management to begin January 2027. Assistant Director of Athletics Communications Athletics / Media & Sports Info - 500380 September 02, 2026 September 16, 2026 Take your athletics communications career to the next level! Tell the stories behind the moments, amplify the achievements of our student-athletes, and help the University of Dayton Flyers take flight. Join Dayton Athletics and make your mark in Division I athletics communications. Apply to our Assistant Director of Athletics Communications opening today! Dining Service Attendant Dining Serv - Kennedy Union - 800613 September 02, 2026 Serve. Connect. Grow. Build Your Future at the University of Dayton.\n\nGreat work environment. Great benefits. Tuition assistance for you and eligible family members. Join our Dining Team and enjoy the opportunity to build your career while investing in your future.\n\nIn this role, you’ll help create a welcoming experience for our students, faculty, staff, and guests by serving customers, stocking and replenishing food and beverages, and maintaining clean and sanitary dining and kitchen areas. Communications Officer Public Safety - 800152 September 01, 2026 September 15, 2026 Join the team that keeps the University of Dayton connected and safe! We are seeking qualified candidates to apply for our Communications Officer (dispatcher) opening! The dispatcher is the primary communication link between community members and officers providing assistance.  This is a full time, benefit eligible position that offers health and dental insurance, retirement, paid time off, tuition assistance for you and your dependents, plus more! Apply today! Parking Services Representative Parking Services - 801355 August 31, 2026 Serving the University community through safety, service, and parking enforcement. Join the University of Dayton as a Parking Services Representative. This is a full-time position that will work Monday to Thursday 11:15 am to 7:45 pm, Friday 8:00 am to 4:30 pm. Apply today! CAD/CAM Programming and Design Specialist/Trainer Advanced Product & Sys Eng - 250615 August 31, 2026 Are you interested in taking your CNC Programing and machining skills to the next level while working for a growing organization? Do you like sharing what you know with others? Do you like to travel? UDRI is seeking a CAD/CAM Programming trainer to assist the Air Force Metal Fabrication and Technologies Office (AFMFTO) with their support of Air Force fabrication shops worldwide. We invite all qualified candidates to apply to this unique opportunity located in Warner Robins Georgia. Advanced Manufacturing Engineer Adv Mfg Engineering - 250714 August 31, 2026 September 11, 2026 Are you interested in working for UDRI, a national leader in scientific and engineering research, serving government, industry and nonprofit customers? UDRI contributes to the fulfillment of the University’s commitments to education, research and public service through the involvement of students, faculty, Staff, and external partners. Established as the research arm of the University of Dayton in 1956, UDRI achieved $2.75 billion in cumulative sponsored research in 2020. We invite qualified candidates to apply for our AM Engineer opening! This full time and benefit eligible position offers health, dental and vision insurance, retirement, disability, tuition assistance for you and your dependents, vacation, sick, and holiday pay. Apply today! Senior Corrosion Testing Lab Tech Applied Sustainment Technology - 250741 August 31, 2026 Join our Warner Robins, GA team and support the research, development, testing, and integration of advanced corrosion prevention materials and processes for USAF aerospace systems and ground support equipment. Apply to our Senior Corrosion Testing Lab Technician opening today! Director, Counseling Center Counseling Center - 700950 August 31, 2026 The University of Dayton, a comprehensive Catholic university in the Marianist tradition, invites applications for the position of Director, Counseling Center. Reporting to the Assistant Vice President for Student Health and Wellbeing, and serving as a member of the Student Development Leadership Team and the Health and Wellbeing Team, the Director of the Counseling Center is responsible for general oversight of an IACS accredited college counseling center and training site for burgeoning practitioners. The University seeks a visionary, innovative, and collaborative leader and strong clinician to lead the Counseling Center which is located within the new Health and Wellbeing Center. To view the position profile, please visit: keelingassociates.com and select ‘Open Searches’. Senior Computer Engineer Scalable Computing - 250642 August 28, 2026 September 11, 2026 Lead the development of high-performance software and embedded systems using C++, Python, MATLAB, FPGAs, and GPUs to advance next-generation U.S. government research missions. Apply to our Senior Computer Engineer opening that the University of Dayton Research Institute today! Associate Data Analyst Sustainment Bus Support Ser - 250723 August 28, 2026 September 11, 2026 Drive the Future of Advanced Manufacturing Through Data-Driven Innovation. In this position, you will be responsible for gathering and analyzing data, reporting performance metrics data to internal management and external clients, determining key performance indicators in current processes, and providing actionable recommendations. Apply to our Associate Data Analyst opening today! Project Analyst Sensor & Software Systems - 250620 August 28, 2026 September 11, 2026 Join the University of Dayton Research Institute (UDRI) as a Project Analyst! In this position, you will report to and work closely with the Principal Project Manager to plan, track and forecast projects across the entire Sensor & Software Systems Division. Apply today! Parking Services Representative Parking Services - 801355 August 27, 2026 Serving the University community through safety, service, and parking enforcement. Join the University of Dayton as a Parking Services Representative. This is a full time position that will work Monday - Friday 2:30 PM - 11:00 PM. Apply today! Catering Event Supervisor Dining Serv - Catering - 800618 August 27, 2026 Join the University of Dayton Catering team and play a key role in bringing exceptional events to life! Lead and support catering staff, coordinate event details, and ensure every guest experience reflects UD’s commitment to outstanding service, teamwork, and excellence. Apply to our Catering Event Supervisor opening today! Full Service Operations Supervisor Dining Serv - Marycrest - 800612 August 27, 2026 Lead the team behind an exceptional campus dining experience! We’re looking for an energetic, dependable leader to oversee daily operations, support and develop staff, ensure quality food and service, and create a welcoming experience for our students and guests. If you enjoy leading people, staying organized, and making things happen in a fast-paced environment, join our team and make an impact every day! Apply to our Full Service Operations Supervisor opening today! Senior Research Engineer High Temp Mtrl Characterization - 250555 August 24, 2026 September 07, 2026 Are you interested in a career opportunity that offers tuition assistance for yourself and dependents, great benefits package, and more? Take the next step in your career and help shape the future of metals research at the renowned University of Dayton Research Institute (UDRI). As a Research Engineer within the Materials Technology and Transition division, you'll work alongside a talented group of researchers to develop cutting-edge technologies that push the boundaries of materials science. Join our cutting-edge team and apply today! Metal AM Researcher Advanced Mfg Tech Development - 250551 August 24, 2026 Shape the future of aerospace defense by leading cutting-edge metal additive manufacturing research at the University of Dayton Research Institute (UDRI).  UDRI is a national leader in scientific and engineering research, serving government, industry and nonprofit customers. Apply to our Metal AM Researcher opening today! More Jobs 69 Current Opportunities To view the position details and/or apply to an open position, click on the position title. All positions close at 11:55 pm EST, unless otherwise noted on the posting. To learn more about our benefits, please click here. Position Department Open Date Close Date Part-Time Catering Services Attendant II Dining Serv - Catering - 800618 September 03, 2026 We are looking for individuals with diverse talents and backgrounds to join our nationally recognized team that is committed to providing exciting and healthy food options to students, faculty and staff on campus. We offer excellent benefits including paid leave and tuition assistance. The University of Dayton is proud to be named the Best Place to Work in the annual Best of Dayton contest. Part-Time Catering Services Attendant I Dining Serv - Catering - 800618 September 03, 2026 We are looking for individuals with diverse talents and backgrounds to join our nationally recognized team that is committed to providing exciting and healthy food options to students, faculty and staff on campus. We 